摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Deeptop, a lightweight native desktop client for DeepSeek Harness.","id":"gh:1333908525","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"DSH-Deeptop","slug":"Sparrived/DSH-Deeptop","topics":["ai-agent","coding-agent","cross-platform","deepseek","deepseek-harness","desktop-app","developer-tools","dsh","dsh-plugin","linux","llm","macos","open-source","react","rust","tauri","typescript","windows"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Deeptop, a lightweight native desktop client for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Deeptop\nHand the complex work to the depths.\nA native desktop workbench built on DeepSeek Harness (D"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"top\nHand the complex work to the depths.\nA native desktop workbench built on DeepSeek Harness (DSH)."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"What is Deeptop ·\nQuick start ·\nDocumentation ·\nDownload ·\nReport an issue"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## What is Deeptop"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"**Deeptop** brings the agent capabilities of DSH into a native desktop environment built for deep wo"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"rk: organize tasks as sessions, ground them in workspaces, and handle tool calls, approvals, follow-"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"up questions and diagnostics right where the work happens."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"It does not put `dsh web` inside a desktop window, nor does it reimplement an agent in the app. DSH "},{"id":"p7s2","text":"remains the source of truth for Agent, Session, Tool, Model, Workspace, Skill, Goal, Provider, persi"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"stence and event semantics; Tauri/Rust owns native windows, process supervision and system capabilit"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ies, and React renders a clear, actionable desktop interface."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> **Desktop first.** Directory picking, file saving and log export go through native Tauri/Bridge ca"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"pabilities; the interface never relies on browser downloads, browser dialogs or internal URLs to per"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"form system operations."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Core experience"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Capability | What you can do |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| **Workspaces & sessions** | Attach working directories with the native directory picker; create, s"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"earch, fork, archive, restore and export sessions. |\n| **Session tray** | See unread and recent sess"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ions in the system tray, reach the rest through “More”, and restore the window straight into a conve"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"rsation; the Windows tray popup has a fixed width and follows Deeptop's light/dark and custom themes"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"tion; the Windows tray popup has a fixed width and follows Deeptop's light/dark and custom themes. |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| **Interactive pets** | Enable an isolated transparent always-on-top pet window that can be dragged"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" across applications and monitors and reacts to taps, long presses and task activity. A shared care "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"layer persists satiety, mood and affection, supports feeding, petting and play, survives skin change"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"s and can be paused independently. The Deeptop activity card can handle a session or switch to the c"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"are panel. Script-free `.deeptop-pet` packs remain separate from care rules and the DSH Bridge, and "},{"id":"p12s6","text":"the master switch destroys the complete pet window. The complete feature can also be removed from so"},{"id":"p12s7","text":"urce with `npm run pets:remove`. |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| **Continuous conversations** | Stream answers and reasoning as they generate; attach images; queue"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" or steer follow-up prompts while a task is running. |\n| **Agent interaction** | Watch tool calls, T"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"odos, Workflows, Jobs and execution trajectories in one place, and answer approvals plus single-choi"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"ce, multi-choice or free-form questions. Clicking a task expands its output: the bridge reads it thr"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"ough DSH's non-consuming projection (`ctx.jobs.peek`), refreshing while the task runs without taking"},{"id":"p13s6","text":" what the model's `job_output` still owns. |\n| **Models & providers** | Browse available providers a"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"nd models, pick the model and reasoning effort per session, and declare Max reasoning for custom pi-"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"ai models; a pi-ai model that declares no thinking levels can also be given Off/Low/Medium/High/Xhig"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"h/Max straight from the composer, which records the declaration in that route's local settings. Cred"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"entials stay managed by the DSH API. |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Native runtime model"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"These boundaries let the desktop reuse DSH's domain contracts instead of dragging the WebUI's browse"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"r lifecycle, download machinery or client-side plugin runtime into a desktop app."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Requirements"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- For local development: Node.js **22.21+** or **24+**, with `node` and `npm` on your `PATH`;\n- Rust"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"/Cargo and the Tauri desktop development environment;\n- A working WebView2 runtime on Windows;\n- Ins"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"tallers bundle a pinned DSH runtime built from pinned sources and never access the npm registry at l"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"s bundle a pinned DSH runtime built from pinned sources and never access the npm registry at launch."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"### Run locally"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"After launch, wait for the embedded DSH runtime to become ready, pick or create a workspace, configu"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"re a provider and credentials, then start your first session. Deeptop launches a pinned DSH build fr"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"om the installer's compressed `dsh-runtime.tar.gz` resource and reuses an extraction cache named aft"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"er the source commit, platform, architecture and runtime tree digest for subsequent starts and updat"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"es; the user's PATH, global npm, npm cache and registry never replace or install the runtime. When n"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"o compatible system Node.js is available, Deeptop downloads the pinned official Node.js 22.21.1 arch"},{"id":"p22s7","text":"ive for that platform (a ZIP on Windows, a tar.gz on Linux and macOS), verifies the compiled SHA-256"},{"id":"p22s8","text":" of both the archive and the extracted executable, and stores only that executable in its app-local "},{"id":"p22s9","text":"runtime cache; it does not modify system PATH or require npm. Runtime builds deploy production depen"},{"id":"p22s10","text":"dencies from `vendor/dsh/pnpm-lock.yaml`; verification compares the archive and resource manifests, "},{"id":"p22s11","text":"recomputes the final archive tree digest, and smoke-loads startup modules including platform-native "},{"id":"p22s12","text":"e final archive tree digest, and smoke-loads startup modules including platform-native dependencies."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"> `npm run dev` only starts a Vite preview without the Tauri Bridge or the DSH subprocess. It is mea"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"nt for layout adjustments, not for verifying session, file or system-integration features."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"### Build & verify"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"| Target | Command |"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Frontend type-check & build | `npm run build` |\n| Generate embedded DSH runtime | `npm run dsh:syn"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"c` |\n| Verify embedded DSH runtime | `npm run dsh:verify` |\n| UI Runtime unit tests | `npm run test:"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"ui-runtime` |\n| Embedded desktop Host UI Runtime acceptance | `npm run test:ui-runtime:host` |\n| Bri"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"dge route tests | `npm run test:bridge` |\n| Full JavaScript test suite | `npm test` |\n| Native app &"},{"id":"p26s5","text":" installers | `npm run tauri:build` |\n| Manifest version consistency | `npm run version:check` |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Document | When to read |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| Project guide | Installation, runtime directories, data flow, extension and troubleshooting. |\n| D"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"SH native coordination | Deciding whether a feature belongs in Tauri, the Bridge, the Profile or Rea"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"ct. |\n| Architecture | Dependency directions, the pure model layer and plugin boundaries. |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
